diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 8256c3b..2c58bed 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -41,3 +41,31 @@ tab to report bugs.
 you can help translate!
 
 If you get stuck or need help with anything at all, head over to the [KDE New Contributors room](https://go.kde.org/matrix/#/#kde-welcome:kde.org) on Matrix. For questions about Breeze, please ask in the [KDE Development room](https://go.kde.org/matrix/#/#kde-devel:kde.org). See [Matrix](https://community.kde.org/Matrix) for more details.
+
+## Window background transparency
+
+This fork installs next to stock Breeze as the **Breeze Transparent** application style and window decoration.
+It only ships the widget style and window decoration (translations are shared with stock Breeze), and
+uses its own configuration file, `~/.config/breezetransparentrc`.
+
+Application windows and dialogs can have a translucent background, optionally blurred by KWin.
+The Breeze Transparent window decoration uses the same opacity for the titlebar and borders.
+Configure it in System Settings → Colors & Themes → Application Style → Breeze Transparent → Transparency, or in `~/.config/breezetransparentrc`:
+
+```ini
+[Common]
+WindowOpacity=85        # 0-100, 100 disables window transparency
+WindowBlurEnabled=true
+
+[Style]
+TranslucentViews=true   # also lists, file views and text editors
+WindowOpacityBlackList=krita,kdenlive   # applications that always stay opaque
+```
+
+Views (lists, trees, text edits) use the same opacity, and so do widgets painting their background
+themselves: the Kate / KWrite text editor and Dolphin's file view. Their background color is turned
+translucent after they painted, the rest (text, icons) is kept.
+
+Enabling transparency (going from 100 to a lower value) requires restarting applications.
+Applications can opt out a single window by setting the `_breeze_no_window_translucency`
+property to `true` on it before it is shown.
